Fortinet rates both flaws at a CVSSv3 base score of 9.8 with a temporal score of 9.1 ([Fortinet FG-IR-26-128](https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-26-128); [Fortinet FG-IR-26-136](https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-26-136)), and 9.1 is the figure ENISA's EUVD records carry ([EUVD-2026-29729](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-29729)). The EUVD records also list FortiAuthenticator 6.4.0 to 6.4.10 and FortiSandbox 4.2.1 to 4.2.8 as affected ([EUVD-2026-29550](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/EUVD-2026-29550)), branches for which Fortinet names no fixed release, and FortiSandbox Cloud 23 and 24 and PaaS 21.3 to 23.4 must migrate to a fixed release ([Fortinet FG-IR-26-136](https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-26-136)). The mitigation Fortinet gives until FortiAuthenticator is upgraded is to disable API access on exposed interfaces under Network, Interfaces, Access Rights ([Fortinet FG-IR-26-128](https://fortiguard.fortinet.com/psirt/FG-IR-26-128)).
